{"availability":"available","full":"Adrianotiger/esp_pwa","name":"esp_pwa","description":"Launch local ESP projects over a PWA.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":5,"forks":1,"created":"2023-03-07T08:09:56Z","updated":"2023-05-16T09:46:20Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://adrianotiger.github.io/esp_pwa/pwa","topics":["control-systems","esp","pwa"],"demo":"https://adrianotiger.github.io/esp_pwa/pwa","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:21.584Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:21.584Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:21.584Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T05:44:21.584Z","stars":5,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An App for your smartphone or desktop to check if an ESP or Arduino is present on the local network, open the IP if available and launch a second PWA to control your device from a remote webpage. => redirect to ESP =>","Every time, you make a Webpage or a simple project with your ESP/Arduino, you have to insert an IP on your browser (example 192.168.1.10). Once it is not available anymore (maybe because you changed board or because it got another IP), you get an error and have to insert a new IP in the address. It is even more complicated if you have a direct link on your home screen.","With this app, you can just insert the IP of your device and when you open it, the app will check if the device is available and will redirect you directly to the device page. The device will then open a second PWA, to control the device over an insecure IP."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Adrianotiger/esp_pwa/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"027bd6eea6a2a2b75f53801b560190d017988a14ab748eabbebbacee9d9a2426","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:21.765Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:21.765Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An App for your smartphone or desktop to check if an ESP or Arduino is present on the l